Benjamin Lewis wrote:

> Is this really a problem?  In my experience, gnomes with wands of death in
> their starting inventory are much more common than gnomes that drop wands
> of death whey they die, but haven't used them.

There is no such thing as a gnome generated with wand of death in his 
inventory. Instead there are gnomes that pick up a wand of death that 
was generated with the level.

If we start to generate random items into monsters inventory then the 
number of these occurences would grow.

> But yes, I for one *do* want that, provided the item in question is one
> that the monster would use if it were in its starting inventory.  I think
> if people don't want particular monsters to use powerful attack wands, then
> either those monsters should *never* use those wands, or they shouldn't be
> generated with them, or drop them when they die.

How many times has your character died with a powerful wand in his 
posession?

Death drop generates random items. I've stated several times that IMHO 
we need a mechanism to generate random items outside the level 
generation. Death drop is one, monster inventory is not one. If we start 
to generate random items into monsters inventory and allow the monster 
to use that item the game becomes more chaotic. Do we want to increase 
the number of YAAD's? I don't.

